  "reason": "Test-only repair of harness, mission and MCP-catalog suites red on origin/main. #939 (831d0d0) made Core storage async but left these tests half converted: await-free helper classes turned into `async create` classmethods still constructed directly, un-awaited prepare_chat (_prepare/_chat_turn), start_chat_turn's producer Task never awaited, sync predicates/stubs over the async store or test client, a missing transaction= keyword, an async def standing in for store.transaction, a double await, asyncio.run inside the loop, threading.Event blocking the loop, and an aiosqlite listener using cursor.connection. Expectations changed on purpose are updated with their commit: #939 applies an idle runtime selection at once (blocked goal stays blocked) and makes catalog/capability reads async; cea8b38 moves selected skills into the standing-instruction snapshot and requires Grok's retained system head (the scripted ACP agents now write it into a temporary account folder); #572 closes the superseded vendor session once idle. Tests held by the host-load gate inject an idle monitor as #1051 does; the API handoff test waits for the background title. Selected: every repaired file, whole where every test passes on the branch, otherwise by node id.",
  "exclusions": "Excluded node ids (each fails or is unsafe for a reason this test-only change does not own): test_harnesses.py::test_explicit_stop_cancels_detached_work_without_completing_it and ::test_stop_closes_a_connection_that_never_acknowledges_interrupt (class b, routed product race G2b: cancel_turn read-then-update races the producer), ::test_harness_transport_error_keeps_one_reference_from_ledger_to_api (class b, routed G2a; unchanged), test_native_hook_turn_ends.py::test_streamed_running_goal_pauses_after_persistent_completion_hook (class b, routed G3a; unchanged), test_grok_acp_compliance.py::test_stop_answers_a_pending_permission_request_with_cancelled (repaired helper, but Stop then hits the routed G2b ConflictError at cancel_turn's HarnessTurn update in 2 of 3 runs), test_harnesses.py::test_browser_attachment_refreshes_catalog_without_replacing_native_thread and ::test_knowledge_access_change_refreshes_fixed_gateway_catalog (repaired async layer; still raise HarnessInstructionContextChanged because cea8b38's channel hash includes gateway tool names, so a catalog change forces a fresh native context, contradicting the resume-the-saved-thread contract these tests encode; reported for an owner decision), ::test_late_approval_decision_does_not_break_the_gateway (repaired; under load a late gateway approval flips the COMPLETE turn to WAITING_APPROVAL because _wait_for_broker_approval updates the turn without a terminal check; passes 3 of 3 alone), test_mcp_catalog_reads.py::test_concurrent_explicit_selections_recheck_idempotency_after_worker_read (repaired; product bug since #939: SubagentService.start now yields between the idempotency check and the insert, so two concurrent starts with one key create two children), test_universal_agent_tools.py::test_harness_child_question_can_wait_for_its_harness_parent (repaired and passing, but every run leaves an aiosqlite query running after the test loop closes (PytestUnhandledThreadExceptionWarning) and one full-file run then hung at interpreter exit), test_harnesses.py::test_chat_gateway_serializes_concurrent_action_calls (not in scope; flaky on main and branch, 1 of 2 each), ::test_active_codex_turn_accepts_steering_with_stale_profile_capabilities (not in scope; fails identically on main and branch), test_missions.py::test_repeated_recovery_approval_interrupts_are_each_persisted (not in scope; its fixed 0.2 s sleep fails under this host's load on main and branch), and test_harness_chat_goals.py::test_operator_interruption_pauses_harness_goal (not in scope, unchanged; its Stop hits the routed G2b ConflictError at cancel_turn's HarnessTurn update in 1 of 3 runs on the branch). test_harness_provider_subagents.py is not selected: #1059 already repaired it, this change does not touch it. No frontend, native or Playwright cases: only Python tests changed. Process-level tests ran with a per-worktree Python 3.12 venv; the five API tests the host-load gate holds on this saturated host ran with the scratch-only pressure shim (not committed).",
